# Rust
debug
/rsworkspace/target/
/rsworkspace/crates/*/*/target/
/target/
# Cargo build output wherever a stray run drops it: a relative CARGO_TARGET_DIR
# builds into ./target from whatever directory cargo was invoked in, which the
# path-anchored rules above do not reach. This repo is public and those artifacts
# embed absolute toolchain paths from the machine that built them.
#
# Matched by the artifacts cargo writes, not by directory name, so a Rust source
# module that happens to be called `target/` stays visible. Directory names in
# the triple glob cannot collide with a module, since Rust identifiers have no
# dashes.
**/target/CACHEDIR.TAG
**/target/.rustc_info.json
**/target/debug/
**/target/release/
**/target/tmp/
**/target/*-*/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.rlib
**/mutants.out*/

